<ShaderNodePreset SupportsAdaptiveDegradation="False" SupportsAction="False" SupportsTransition="False" SupportsTimeline="False" TimelineUseBack="False" MatteProvider="True" CommercialUsePermitted="True" ShaderType="Matchbox" SoftwareVersion="2016.0.0" LimitInputsToTexture="True" Version="1" Description="Block style drop shadow. Extrudes the matte along an angle, or towards a vanishing point, to create a solid shadow, which can be set back from the fill, shaded along its length, softened and outlined. The fill (Front or a colour) is comped over it. The shadow can be coloured with a flat colour or the optional Shadow Fill input. Outputs premultiplied RGB and the combined matte. Written by Andrew Miller (andrew.miller@mtifilm.com)." HelpLink="https://github.com/andrew-m-miller/block-shadow" Name="BlockShadow">
